## Obsidian community plugin

This project is an Obsidian community plugin, scaffolded from the canonical
[obsidian-sample-plugin](https://github.com/obsidianmd/obsidian-sample-plugin).
TypeScript in `src/` is bundled by esbuild into `main.js`, which Obsidian loads.

- Package manager: **npm** (`package.json` scripts, `package-lock.json`). Never bun or pnpm.
- Bundler: **esbuild** (`esbuild.config.mjs`). Types come from the `obsidian` package.
- Release artifacts: `main.js`, `manifest.json`, and `styles.css` (optional).

### Commands

```bash
npm install          # dev dependencies, pinned by the committed package-lock.json
npm run dev          # watch build -> main.js (inline sourcemaps)
npm run build        # type-check, then production build
npm run lint         # eslint with eslint-plugin-obsidianmd
mise run plugin:link # symlink this repo into $OBSIDIAN_VAULT/.obsidian/plugins/<id>
```

Reload Obsidian (or use the Hot-Reload plugin) and enable the plugin under
**Settings → Community plugins**.

### Layout

- `src/main.ts` stays small: plugin lifecycle (`onload`/`onunload`) and registration only.
- Feature logic goes in focused modules under `src/` (`settings.ts`, `commands/`, `ui/`, `utils/`).
- Never commit `node_modules/`, `main.js`, `*.map`, or the vault's `data.json`.
- Bundle every runtime dependency into `main.js`; keep dependencies small and browser-compatible.

### Manifest rules (`manifest.json`)

- `id` is stable API: never change it after release. It must not contain "obsidian",
  and for local development it must match the plugin folder name in the vault.
- `version` is SemVer `x.y.z`; keep `minAppVersion` accurate when you use newer APIs.
- `isDesktopOnly` must be `true` if you use Node or Electron APIs.
- Canonical checks: https://github.com/obsidianmd/obsidian-releases/blob/master/.github/workflows/validate-plugin-entry.yml

### Versioning and releases

- `npm version patch|minor|major` is the release step. It bumps `package.json`, and
  `version-bump.mjs` syncs `manifest.json` and `versions.json` (plugin version → minimum
  app version). It commits, then tags the bare version: no leading `v`, because `.npmrc`
  sets `tag-version-prefix=""`.
- `mise run version:bump` keeps the same three files in step without committing or tagging.
- Push the tag. `.github/workflows/release.yml` drafts the GitHub release with `main.js`,
  `manifest.json` and `styles.css` attached.
- The community catalog requires a public repo and a LICENSE; pick one before submitting.

### Plugin conventions

- Add commands with `this.addCommand(...)` and stable IDs; never rename a released ID.
- Persist settings with `this.loadData()` / `this.saveData()`, with defaults in `settings.ts`.
- Register every DOM event, workspace event, and interval through `this.register*`,
  so the plugin unloads without leaking listeners.
- Keep `onload` light: defer heavy work, debounce vault events, batch disk access.
- Stay inside the vault, make no network calls without a user-visible reason, and never
  fetch or eval remote code. These are Obsidian's developer policies, and review enforces them.
- UI copy uses sentence case, short imperative labels, and **Settings → Community plugins**
  style arrow navigation.

References: [API docs](https://docs.obsidian.md) ·
[Plugin guidelines](https://docs.obsidian.md/Plugins/Releasing/Plugin+guidelines) ·
[Developer policies](https://docs.obsidian.md/Developer+policies)
